    "title": "Culver City Police Station Temporarily Transformed Into LAPD Station for Film Shoot - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Current Staff ,\n20 hours ago CULVER CITY - Culver City police got a temporary identity change this week when their station was dressed up to look like an LAPD facility for a film shoot.\nA production placed a \"Los Angeles Police Dept.\" sign outside the building and transformed the station's exterior and lobby into an LAPD set. \"\nIf you drove by today and thought you were suddenly in a different city, you were not alone,\" Culver City police wrote Wednesday.\nThe department said it has not moved or rebranded and remains fully operational, serving Culver City around the clock.\nThe LAPD sign is expected to remain outside the station for the next few days.\n\"No rebrand. No move. Just a little movie magic,\" the department said.",
    "summary": "20 hours ago CULVER CITY - Culver City police got a temporary identity change this week when their station was dressed up to look like an LAPD facility for a film shoot. A production placed a \"Los Angeles Police Dept.\" sign outside the building and transformed the station's exterior and lobby into an LAPD set. \" The department said it has not moved or rebranded and remains fully operational, serving Culver City around the clock. The LAPD sign is expected to remain outside the station for the next few days.",
